isk (5/10).","financial_summary":["Industrial Logistics Properties is a small-cap real estate business with a $407M market cap.","Returns on capital run at 3% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $42M in free cash flow, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 13.3\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 0.5\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 2.1% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 17% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.1) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Payout ratio of 92% leaves thin coverage if earnings wobble","sev":"amber","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 78/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Real Estate peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Real Estate peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Interest-rate sensitivity and tenant-credit risk \u2014 cap rates and refinancing costs move faster than the 10-year leases can absorb.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Trading Systems Reacting to (ILPT) Volatility","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/9/Trading_Systems_Reacting_to_ILPT_Volatility_110726012601_1794075961.html","date":"2026-11-07","timestamp":1794075961.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Industrial Logistics Properties Trust (NASDAQ:ILPT) Stock Gets Price Target Reduction from Freedom Broker","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/industrial-logistics-properties-trust-nasdaqilpt-stock-gets-price-target-reduction-from-freedom-broker.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793954223.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.953,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["analyst_action"]},{"title":"Industrial Logistics Properties Trust (NASDAQ:ILPT) Given New $10.00 Price Target at B. Riley Financial","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/02/industrial-logistics-properties-trust-nasdaqilpt-given-new-10-00-price-target-at-b-riley-financial.html","date":"2026-11-02","timestamp":1793640290.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.872,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["analyst_action"]},{"title":"Industrial Logistics Properties Trust (NASDAQ:ILPT) Releases FY 2026 Earnings Guidance","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/10/30/industrial-logistics-properties-trust-nasdaqilpt-releases-fy-2026-earnings-guidance.html","date":"2026-10-30","timestamp":1793373048.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.937,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","guidance"]},{"title":"Industri